          "content": "How Quantities Combine: Understanding Data"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.853,
            0.071,
            0.881,
            0.087
          ],
          "content": "17"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.11,
            0.881,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": "whether there are more male langurs or more female langurs? Or are they equal in number?"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.303,
            0.166,
            0.74,
            0.327
          ],
          "content": "|  | Male langurs | Female langurs | All langurs |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Average weight | 16.5 kg | 13.8 kg | 14.925 kg |\n| Number of langurs |  |  | 60 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_9_table_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.351,
            0.881,
            0.39
          ],
          "content": "(i) Which of the following expression(s) describes the scenario?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.242,
            0.401,
            0.526,
            0.442
          ],
          "content": "(a) $\\frac{16.5x + 13.8y}{x + y} = 14.925$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.242,
            0.447,
            0.544,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": "(b) $\\frac{16.5x + 13.8y}{60} = -14.925$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.244,
            0.491,
            0.541,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{16.5x + 13.8y}{2} = - 14.925",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.242,
            0.536,
            0.543,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": "(d) $\\frac{16.5x + 13.8y}{16.5 + 13.8} = -14.925$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.584,
            0.732,
            0.604
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Find out how many male langurs are present."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.604,
            0.882,
            0.66
          ],
          "content": "(iii) A female langur weighing 15.2 kg is admitted to the facility. What is the average weight of the female langurs after this?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.66,
            0.881,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": "(iv) Two male langurs weighing 16.9 kg and 16.1 kg are released from the facility. What is the average weight of the male langurs after this?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.19,
            0.718,
            0.882,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": "(v) Now, suppose one of the male langurs lost 1 kg of weight. What is the average weight of all the male langurs after this?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.786,
            0.884,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": "8. Dorjee has collected 1 litre of water from the Dead Sea! Using the information in the table, answer the following questions. A calculator can be used if necessary."
        }
      ]
    }
